  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::TitleScreenController
  titlePanel: {fileID: 1165493736}
  cutscenePanel: {fileID: 932858319}
  cutsceneImage: {fileID: 1330879218}
  cutsceneCaptionText: {fileID: 1059644194}
  cutsceneImages:
  - {fileID: 0}
  cutsceneCaptions:
  - On the morning of December 30, 1896, a man stood before the guns of an empire.
  - His hands were bound, but his mind remained free.
  - "Jos\xE9 Rizal, reformist, physician, writer, son of Calamba, had been condemned
    as a traitor."
  - Yet before the final shot could silence him, his life had already spoken louder
    than any weapon.
  - To understand why a man of peace was feared by those in power, we must return
    to the fire that first awakened his generation.
  - Years before Rizal faced the rifles at Bagumbayan, three priests walked toward
    their own deaths.
  - In their final moments, a nation still asleep began to stir.
  captionDurations:
  - 8
  - 5
  - 10
  - 8
  - 12
  - 7
  - 7
